# CloudFormation vs Terraform ⭐⭐⭐

This is a very important DevOps interview question.

### CloudFormation

```text
AWS
 ↓
CloudFormation
 ↓
AWS Resources
```

CloudFormation is an **AWS-native IaC service**.

### Terraform

```text
Terraform
   ↓
AWS
Azure
GCP
Kubernetes
etc.
```

Terraform is a **multi-cloud IaC tool**.

### Comparison

| Feature | CloudFormation | Terraform |
|---|---|---|
| Developed by | AWS | HashiCorp |
| IaC | ✅ | ✅ |
| AWS support | Excellent | Excellent |
| Multi-cloud | Limited | ✅ |
| Template language | YAML/JSON | HCL |
| AWS-native | ✅ | ❌ |
| State file | Managed by CloudFormation | Terraform state |
| Drift detection | Supported | Terraform has planning/state-based workflows |
| Community ecosystem | AWS-focused | Large multi-provider ecosystem |

For an AWS-focused environment, CloudFormation is a very natural choice.

For multi-cloud infrastructure, Terraform is often preferred.

